{#
  The small padlock beside a link a signed-out visitor is shown but cannot use
  yet (owner, 13 Nov 2026). Which links carry it is decided in
  lib/accessible-shell.js (`signInRequired` -> `locked`); this is only the mark.

  Call it INSIDE the link, straight after the label with NO space between:
    <a href="…">{{ label }}{{ signInLock(t("home.module_signin_hint")) }}</a>
  A space there is underlined along with the link text and leaves a stray
  line under the gap. The gap comes from the stylesheet, and the pause a
  screen reader needs comes from the space inside the hidden words.

  - The picture is decoration (aria-hidden); the words carry the meaning, so
    the link's name reads "Members Sign in to use this." to a screen reader.
    The wording is the home page's existing hint, already in eleven languages.
  - Drawn with currentColor, so it follows the link's own colour through hover,
    focus and visited, and needs no contrast rule of its own.
  - width/height are set on the element as well as in CSS, so it stays small if
    the stylesheet fails to load.
  - A plain padlock outline: no crown, no GOV.UK identity (brand:check).
#}
{% macro signInLock(words) -%}
<svg class="nexus-alpha-lock" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="13" height="13" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><rect x="4" y="11" width="16" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 11V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v4"/></svg><span class="govuk-visually-hidden"> {{ words }}</span>
{%- endmacro %}
